{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>But the spelt and the wheat.</b> Late-growing, and they were still soft and able to withstand a hard blow. And even though it is said, ״וְאֵת כָּל עֵשֶׂב הַשָּׂדֶה הִכָּה הַבָּרָד״, the plain sense of Scripture is to be explained of the grasses standing in their stalk, fit to be struck by hail. And in the midrash of Rabbi Tanchuma there are some of our Rabbis who disagreed with this and expounded <b>כי אפילת</b> — wondrous signs were done for them, that they were not struck."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:17.265314075Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}